    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2518\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize the commissioner of general services to transfer\nand convey certain land to the Kings Park fire district\n\n\n PURPOSE OF LEGISLATION :\n\nTo direct the Commissioner of General Services to transfer\napproximately 5 acres of the former Kings Park Psychiatric Center\nproperty to the Kings Park Fire District to enhance public safety.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe former Kings Park Psychiatric Center has passed through a number\nof different evolutions and decisions about its future in the past few\nyears. At every stage there has always been a small parcel of the\nproperty reserved for the Kings Park Fire District. Now that the\nproperty is under the jurisdiction of the Parks Department, this bill\nseeks to conclude the formal transfer of the parcel to the fire\ndistrict which will benefit general public and the fire district in a\nnumber of ways.\n\nThe local community has learned through experience that a fire station\ncan, by the nature of the business, be a noisy neighbor even trying to\nbe considerate. The larger 5-acre property will permit a buffer that\nwill help the district to be good neighbors. It will also enable them\nto develop the property in a way that blends in with the surrounding\narea and provide setbacks to soften the impact of the site.\n\nThe National Fire Prevention Association Standards now require that\nfire apparatus have fully enclosed cabs for maximum firefighter\nsafety. This requirement alone has lengthened fire apparatus by an\nadditional 10 to 12 feet, bringing the average length of equipment to\n37 feet. As a result, the most cost efficient way to construct a new\nfire station is to construct double bays in depth with access and\negress from both sides. This manner of construction will necessitate\nthat the building be approximately 100 feel in depth. After allowing\nfor safety ramps in front of each apparatus bay, and also allowing for\nthe turning radius on the apparatus which is approximately 47 feet, it\nwould necessitate the parcel being larger to accommodate the new foot\nprint for the building. In addition, it will be necessary to locate\nemergency power generation equipment on the parcel and to be able to\nprovide adequate parking around the station for emergency responder\npersonnel.\n\nThe parcel is also strategically located for the fire district and the\ncommunity. It will provide reduced response time into the San Remo\ncommunity and is also situated on the only other eastwest roadway that\nextends from one end of the fire district to the other.\n\nLastly, this parcel will afford the fire district the ability to meet\ntoday's needs and the flexibility to expand in the future when\nwarranted.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
